# Docker build context for the repo-root builds (gateway + ai_service).
# Without this the daemon would receive .tools/ (portable PostgreSQL, JDK, Android SDK),
# backend/.venv and web/node_modules — gigabytes of build context per build.
# backend/Dockerfile and web/Dockerfile use their own, smaller contexts.

# Version control
.git
.github
.gitignore

# Secrets and local state — must never enter an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example
*.key
data/
.backups/

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Node / web (built separately with the ./web context)
**/node_modules
web/dist
web/test-results
web/playwright-report

# Local tooling and scratch data
.tools/
pgdata/
*.log

# Not needed by any runtime image
mobile/
docs/
ontology/          # mounted at runtime instead (SISI_ONTOLOGY_DIR)
README.md
LICENSE
AGENTS.md
*.md
